# One browser

Every chat uses the same Google Chrome. It is the `user-playwright` MCP. The launcher opens that Chrome once; the next chat attaches to it.

Profile: `/Users/embatron/Projects/adminvps-billing-clean/.cursor/playwright-profile`.
Launcher: `scripts/mcp-playwright-start.sh` in that project. It listens on `127.0.0.1:9333`.

The everyday Chrome window is a different profile. Leave it alone.

## Do

- Call tools on `user-playwright`.
- List tabs first. Open the page in a tab that is already there.
- Leave the window open when the task ends.

## Do not

```ts
// wrong: a second browser, or closing the shared window
// cursor-ide-browser, plugin-playwright, Chrome for Testing, --isolated
browser_close();

// right
browser_tabs({ action: "list" });
```

`npm` Playwright tests keep the bundled headless Chromium. They do not use this window.
